/*
  AssocIcons.rc - the two file-association icons, carried INSIDE Avro Keyboard.exe.

  An .avrolayout or .avroskin file takes its Explorer icon from
  Software\Classes\AvroKeyboardLayout\DefaultIcon (respectively
  AvroKeyboardSkin\DefaultIcon), which the installer points at Avro
  Keyboard.exe with a NEGATIVE index: the absolute value is the RT_GROUP_ICON
  resource id below, not a position in the file.  A positive index would mean
  "the nth icon group in the executable", and index 0 has to stay the
  application's own icon - the .AvroEnco association and the uninstall entry
  both use it.

  The artwork is the same pair the installer used to drop into {app} as loose
  .ico files (extracted from the original Avro Keyboard's own resources:
  ZZKLICON = keyboard for .avrolayout, ZZSKICON = window skin for .avroskin).
  The install folder is to carry no loose .ico files, so the icons are linked
  into the binary instead - exactly how Layout\AvroBaseline.res, Layout\
  Internal_Layout.res and Skin\Internal_Skin.res carry their payloads.

  Compile from this folder with:
    brcc32 -fo"AssocIcons.res" "AssocIcons.rc"

  The path is relative to the compiler's working directory (this folder).  The
  .res is a committed input, so a build links it without having to run brcc32.
*/

101 ICON "..\..\assets\icons\AssocLayout.ico"
102 ICON "..\..\assets\icons\AssocSkin.ico"
